This code generator produces one ``${output_file}`` file from a :doc:`../buml_language/model_types/structural`:
each class of the model, with its attributes and their types.

Create a ``${class_name}`` with the model and call its ``generate`` method:

.. code-block:: python

    from besser.generators.${name} import ${class_name}

    generator = ${class_name}(model=library_model)
    generator.generate()

The file is written to the ``output`` folder of the current directory, or to ``output_dir`` when one is given.
